{"id": "EUVD-2026-59265", "enisaUuid": "c09782c5-bc74-37e7-8b01-df41faca40ab", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: Fix netfs_create_write_req() to handle async cache object creation\n\nnetfs_create_write_req() will skip caching if the fscache cookie is\ndisabled, but this is a problem because async cache object creation might\nnot have got far enough yet that has been enabled - thereby causing the\ncall to fscache_begin_write_operation() to be skipped.\n\nFix this by removing the checks on the cookie and delegating this to\nfscache_begin_write_operation().", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:41", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aee03fbc8803a40d65e20f1af816a7219048a426", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ab75e445c161c4cb504aa98e20ce1dd1ecd8e9a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1188a9846fadeacf9d1430b528e5217f749d665b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbd6f56d975b23241b7bbb11bb8f562af548a0aa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8q2x-69cw-5m48", "CVE-2026-72366"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16716ea7-45f4-3ca9-aa32-718ea52c00bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "1d8d9707-1cc3-3ef9-839e-307ac85f6b4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b589a9b45ae32aa9d7bece597490e141198d7a6 <1188a9846fadeacf9d1430b528e5217f749d665b"}, {"id": "337177cf-3c09-3bba-8e41-8fe5e9e8eb2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "8acf8453-bb69-34b7-9943-d6039808cbc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "96b7dc11-ef9c-34df-ae2d-fb38697a233a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7b58